Odd-Even Merge Sort在MNM Top-k Selector中的执行流程：```// Full Sorter: Odd-Even Merge Sort for 16 new distances
Input: d[0..15] (16 distances from PQ code scanners) with reordered IDs
// Stage 1: Sort 16 elements using odd-even merge sort network
for step in 0..log2(16)-1:
    for each pair (i, i+2^step) in parallel:
        if d[i] > d[i+2^step]:
            swap(d[i], d[i+2^step])
// After full sort: d[0] <= d[1] <= ... <= d[15]

// Partial Sorter: Merge sorted d[0..15] with top-16 register
Input: d_sorted[0..15], top_reg[0..15] (previous top-16 results)
// Merge two sorted 16-element sequences using merge network
Output: merged[0..31] (sorted 32 elements)
// Select smallest 16 from merged:
top_reg_new[0..15] = merged[0..15]
// Update top-k register with new distances and associated codeword IDs
```。Hardware实现特性：(1) Full sorter和Partial sorter均基于Odd-Even Merge Sort network，每个stage内所有compare-and-swap操作并行执行→constant O(log²N) latency per sort cycle；(2) 16个scanner每cycle产生16个distances→Full sorter sorting latency固定（与数据分布无关）→deterministic pipeline timing；(3) Partial sorter merge使得per-cluster processing的intermediate results保持compact（仅top-16 distances + IDs需要存储，而非所有codewords的distances）。

